# Desktop run controls and layout
Workstream-ID: lea-11
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/11
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed desktop usability and run-control implementation
Status: DONE
Milestone: A usable desktop front end with complete supported run controls
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Make the native desktop application usable without memorizing CLI switches or
editing YAML for common run settings. Keep the existing automation engine and
DeepSeaFoam/Harbor Daylight palettes, and do not submit applications during
development or qualification.

## Tasks
- [x] Reconcile the GUI with the actual CLI and configuration contracts.
- [x] Provide a scrollable setup panel, readable live output and command preview.
- [x] Expose retry listing, connection-run filtering and interactive input.
- [x] Expose common search, cap, browser and behavior settings as run-local overrides.
- [x] Confirm every action capable of real submissions or invitations.
- [x] Exercise widget signals and subprocess input/output with offline fixtures.
- [x] Review rendered dark/light and smaller-window layouts with synthetic data.
- [x] Update the user guide and safe screenshots.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Supported CLI run switches have usable GUI controls with action-specific states.
- [x] Per-submit and unknown-question prompts can be answered without a terminal.
- [x] Run-local settings preserve the saved configuration and other unedited values.
- [x] Real Apply, Reapply and Connect actions require explicit confirmation.
- [x] No personal configuration, browser session or live application is used for captures.
- [x] Focused tests and required quality checks pass for the delivered source.

## Completion evidence
Implemented scrollable run setup, wrapped output, terminal input, safe command
preview and action-specific Apply/Scan/Reapply/Connect controls. Search, limits,
browser and behavior overrides are validated into private run presets without
overwriting saved configuration. Configuration saves preserve unsaved Answers.
Eight regenerated screenshots use isolated fictional data. The README embeds
all eight desktop views with captions, including expanded run settings and
the compact light-theme layout.

Whole-repository Ruff, release-scoped Black, mypy over 69 product files and all
681 tests passed in the exact-source hosted Windows qualification. The portable GUI/CLI also passed
offline rendering, stream/input and child-command smoke checks. Human aesthetic
acceptance and live LinkedIn qualification are not claimed. Release publication
and exact downloaded-binary verification belong to lea-12.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-08: Compared the existing five-page GUI with actual CLI signatures.
  Found missing controls and disabled per-submit confirmation with no input channel.
- 2026-11-08: Completed the bounded desktop implementation and offline checks.
  Corrected partial output handling, shared validation and unsaved-answer retention.
  No live application, invitation or private browser session was used.
- 2026-11-08: Updated the README's v0.2.0 gallery with captioned expanded
  run settings and the 980-by-680 layout, alongside both themes and all five
  pages. Captures are explicitly fictional source-install previews.
